.*%METADATA                                                            *
.* %TEXT help panel group for XMLPREVIEW command        jcr            *
.*%EMETADATA                                                           *
.*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
.* XMLPREVIEW - Easy view of XML upload member - Help Text             *
.* By   Craig Rutledge,  7/18/2001                                   *
.*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
:PNLGRP.
:HELP name='XMLPREVIEW/ALL'.
:IMHELP name=XMLPREVIEW.
:IMHELP name='XMLPREVIEW/UPLOADMBR'.
:IMHELP name='XMLPREVIEW/UPLOADSRCF'.
:IMHELP name='XMLPREVIEW/OUTPUTSRCF'.
:EHELP.
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP NAME='XMLPREVIEW'.
View XML Upload Members (XMLPREVIEW) - Help
:P.
This command reads an uploaded source member, listing the members
and commands to be executed, into a subfile for easy review.
:EHELP.
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* HELP TEXT FOR XMLKEY PARAMETER
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='XMLPREVIEW/UPLOADMBR'.
Uploaded member name  - Help
:XH3.Uploaded member name (UPLOADMBR)
:P.
Specifies the member name of a uploaded member
that contains the source and object information about to be installed.
:P.
This is a required parameter.
:PARML.
:PT.member-name
:PD.Specify the uploaded member name.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* HELP TEXT FOR UPLOADSRCF
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='XMLPREVIEW/UPLOADSRCF'.
Uploaded into source file - Help
:XH3.Uploaded into source file (UPLOADSRCF)
:P.Specifies the name of the source file where the upload member was
placed.
.*
:PARML.
:PT.source-file-name
:PD.Enter the source file name for the upload member.
.*
:PT.:PK def.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The system searches the library list to find the library where the
source file is located.
.*
:PT.library-name
:PD.Enter the name of the library where the source file is located.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* HELP TEXT FOR OUTSRCPF
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='XMLPREVIEW/OUTPUTSRCF'.
Output to this source file - Help
:XH3.Output to this source file  (OUTPUTSRCF)
:P.Optionally specifies the name of the source file where ALL  members will be
extracted.  This option is available to persons who want install all
source members into a single selected source file.  This option can
only be used if the uploaded file has different names for all members.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK def.*DEFAULTS:EPK.
:PD.The default source files, defined in the uploaded member, will be used.
.*
:PT.source-file-name
:PD.Enter the source file name to contain the extracted source members.
Source file does not have to exists as it will be created.
Note:  To use this option you must verfiy
the uploaded text has no duplicate member names.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
.*
:EPNLGRP.
